  data:  # 32fb
    kind: invariant  # 32fb
    title: "A tracker sync must never commit a net deletion of an existing .ops file"  # 32fb
    status: violated  # 32fb
    priority: 1  # 32fb
    parent:  # 32fb
    tags:  # 32fb
    - wave0  # 32fb
    isbefore: []  # 32fb
    duplicate_of: []  # 32fb
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 32fb
    pr_ref:  # 32fb
    description: ""  # 32fb
    fields:  # 32fb
      statement: "Tracker .ops files are append-only op-logs. A `tracker sync` must never produce a commit that DELETES an .ops file present on origin/dev. When the sync builds its commit from a stale/incomplete working tree (e.g. local dev behind origin, files dropped by an intervening branch checkout), the absent files are silently recorded as deletions and the items vanish from the corpus."  # 32fb
      root_cause: "Five-step chain: (1) a tracker-sync commit (d77dd0a368) lands WI-vojik/WI-durub .ops on origin/dev; (2) local dev stays behind (forge flakiness blocked the early sync; the transient-405 stopped auto-pr cleanup_local from advancing local dev); (3) PR #1 auto-pr rebases the feature branch onto origin/dev, making those .ops tracked-in-feature; (4) a manual `git checkout dev` to the stale local dev DELETES them (tracked-in-source, absent-in-target); (5) the next sync builds its commit from the now-incomplete tree on top of up-to-date origin/dev and records a deletion (ef26ed9824). sync.py has no guard that a sync is additive w.r.t. .ops FILES. Data was fully recoverable from d77dd0a368."  # 32fb
