- op: discuss  # b524
  at: '2026-06-11T21:49:18Z'  # b524
  by: agent  # b524
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b524
  clock: 3  # b524
  nonce: b524  # b524
  message: "Fixed in PR #4197 (merged; origin/dev c541b72356). Both staging sites in do_sync now route through _stage_tracker_ops_additive, which passes `git add --ignore-removal` (stage additions/modifications only, never removals). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: test_stage_tracker_ops_additive_keeps_oplog_missing_from_worktree drives the real read-tree -> additive-add -> write-tree sequence in a temp git repo: an op-log committed in the base but DELETED from the working tree SURVIVES in the written tree (`.WI-keep.ops` present), while a new op-log is still added (`.WI-new.ops` present) — i.e. the sync can no longer commit the deletion that lost WI-vojik/WI-durub. A mock test pins do_sync passes --ignore-removal (red on plain add). sync.py at 100% coverage; 1813 passed. The lost items themselves were recovered intact from git d77dd0a368."  # b524
